NOTE: 'seconds' is now the touched-files-only cost, because -E kept
mutation inside the touched set. It still includes gremlins' own
whole-package coverage pass, which -E does not scope: gremlins runs
`go test -cover -coverprofile <f> ./<pkg>/...` once per package
before generating a mutant, with no -timeout flag, so Go's
unconfigurable 10-minute default applies to that pass.
